  "hashAlgorithm": "blake2b-256",
  "body": {
    "summary": "We have determined that this Parameter Change governance action is constitutional.",
    "rationaleStatement": "Article II, Section 6.3 of the Cardano Constitution states \"\"Hard Fork Initiation\" and \"Parameter Update\" actions shall undergo sufficient technical review and scrutiny as mandated by the Guardrails to ensure that the governance action does not endanger the security, functionality, performance, or long-term sustainability of the Cardano Blockchain.\"\n\nThe governance action with ID “gov_action1cadmygtqv6r64pvwezw859wg36wpwp209cz94cc7ej9fdp7dyphqq58n5ur” and title “Reduce the committeeMinSize parameter from 7 to 5”, as a Parameter Change governance action, has “undergone appropriate technical review and scrutiny through the Parameter Committee Parameter Change Process (PCP)” and states that it “does not endanger the security, functionality, performance, or long-term sustainability of the Cardano Blockchain.”\n\nThe governance action complies with the relevant guardrails, being CMS-01, CMS-02 and CMS-03.  It also provides a Reversion Plan as required by Appendix I, Section 2.6.\n\nWe therefore find this governance action **Constitutional**.",
    "precedentDiscussion": "None",
    "counterargumentDiscussion": "None",
    "conclusion": "As a Parameter Change, this governance action has undergone sufficient technical review and complies with the relevant guardrails in the Cardano Constitution, so is deemed constitutional.",
    "internalVote": {
      "constitutional": 4,
      "unconstitutional": 0,
      "abstain": 2,
      "didNotVote": 1
    },
    "references": []
  },
